  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">End Child Marriages for 2000 Young Girls in Malawi</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will bring back to school 2000 girls from two districts in Malawi who were forced into child marriages due to harmful traditional and religious practices and peer pressure. Social Development and Advocacy Centre (SODAC) will work with the Government of Malawi to protect young girls from child marriage and other harmful practices by increasing knowledge and understanding among traditional/religious/community leaders on the harm associated with child marriages and teenage pregnancies.</narrative>
  </description>
